alysis_taxicab_metric_4686b892_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In $(\\mathbb{R}^2,d_1)$ with the taxicab metric, what does the set $\\{(x,y)\\colon x^2+y^2=1\\}$ look like?","options":["A diamond","A square","Four isolated points","A circle"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"527e7778b0910dd2aa4d3470","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_taxicab_metric_4686b892_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What movement idea motivates the taxicab metric?","options":["Moving like a chess king, with diagonal steps costing one unit","Moving through the shortest Euclidean line segment","Moving diagonally whenever possible to shorten the trip","Moving along coordinate directions rather than diagonally"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2c15a052330af09046baab66","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_taxicab_metric_4686b892_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $d_1((0,0),(3,4))$ in $\\mathbb{R}^2$?","options":["$5$","$12$","$1$","$7$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b954e4f6e21fcfc55ac21385","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_taxicab_metric_4686b892_011_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"The vectors $\\boldsymbol{u}=(1,0)$ and $\\boldsymbol{v}=(\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})$ both have Euclidean norm $1$, and $\\boldsymbol{v}$ is $\\boldsymbol{u}$ rotated by $45^\\circ$. Which statement about their taxicab norms is correct?","options":["$\\|\\boldsymbol{u}\\|_1=1$ and $\\|\\boldsymbol{v}\\|_1=\\sqrt{2}$: the taxicab norm depends on the chosen axes.","$\\|\\boldsymbol{u}\\|_1=\\|\\boldsymbol{v}\\|_1=1$: rotating a vector never changes a norm.","$\\|\\boldsymbol{u}\\|_1=1$ and $\\|\\boldsymbol{v}\\|_1=1/\\sqrt{2}$: the taxicab norm takes the largest coordinate.","$\\|\\boldsymbol{u}\\|_1=\\|\\boldsymbol{v}\\|_1=\\sqrt{2}$: in $\\mathbb{